"Internal Error ()\nciteturn41219view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://zenodo.org/records/23382634\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: URL https://zenodo.org/records/23382634 is not accessible via this tool.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn41219view1 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://api.datacite.org/dois/10.5281/zenodo.23382634\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: URL https://api.datacite.org/dois/10.5281/zenodo.23382634 is not accessible via this tool.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2610.22820] Causal Edit Serialization (https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22820)\nciteturn41219view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22820\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 166\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computation and Language\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 16 Oct 2026]\nL9: # Title:Causal Edit Serialization\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Louis Robinson L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Causal Edit Serialization, by Louis Robinson\nL14: \nL15: cite6†View PDF cite7†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Standard autoregressive language models generate text sequentially, but revision requires referring back to tokens in the input context or those already generated. Causal Edit Serialization (CES) is introduced as a framework for expressing such revisions within the same causal token stream. Special pointer tokens are paired with predicted source addresses, allowing insertion, deletion, replacement, copying and movement to be localized explicitly.\nL17: A lightweight localization head and dual-index rotary position encoding support both address prediction and conditioning on previously emitted pointers, while retaining a standard causal attention mask. A pretraining procedure combines ordinary language modeling with serialized repairs derived from random corruptions, model-generated edits and repeated text.\nL18: Across model scales and editing baselines, CES models demonstrate complete applied edits with modestly higher clean-text bits per byte than clean autoregressive models. Supervised and reinforcement-learning post-training provide a grammatical-error-correction proof of concept, producing more beneficial than harmful changes under reference-blind model judging. Correct repair programs also improve subsequent text prediction while the original context and its cached states are retained.\nL19: CES provides a common interface for generation and localized revision, with potential extensions to iterative refinement and additional pointer-addressed transformations.\nL20: Comments:  | 37 pages, including appendices and checklist. Code: cite8†this https URL†github.com ; data and checkpoints: cite9†this https URL†huggingface.co L21: Subjects:  | Computation and Language (cs.CL); Machine Learning (cs.LG)\nL22: Cite as:  | cite10†arXiv:2610.22820 [cs.CL]\nL23:    | (or cite11†arXiv:2610.22820v1 [cs.CL] for this version)\nL24:    | cite12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2610.22820†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite (pending registration)\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Louis Robinson [cite13†view email ]\nL28: [v1] Fri, 16 Oct 2026 01:55:26 UTC (516 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled Causal Edit Serialization, by Louis Robinson\nL35: \nL36:   * cite6†View PDF L37:   * cite7†HTML (experimental) L38:   * cite14†TeX Source L39: \nL40: cite15†view license†creativecommons.org L41: \nL42: ### Additional Features\nL43: \nL44:   * cite16†Audio S